==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Crazed Macho Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Manic Mohawk Cat''' when obtained from [[Deathhawk (Deadly)|Cat Maniac]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
The good thing about faster meatshields is that it takes them less time to arrive at the front line, allowing you to fill in the space between your units and enemy units quicker, preventing enemy advancement as a result. Therefore, you could survive a surprise enemy assault with this unit. Improved speed also helps it reach the frontline quicker, which reduced the amount of cats you have which helps in long stages where max amount of cats can be annoying. Otherwise, the crazed cat is just a speedy meatshield that tends to be killed in a hit or 2, designed to be a sacrifice.

He can be a very good staller in [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]] of the [[Heavenly Tower]], where he can be used to stall Hermit Cat efficiently and keep him there. This is also true for [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 40|Floor 40]] against Yulala, but you'll need to have extreme reflexes and its true form.

As a meatshield he is outclassed by [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]] and especially in its true form, as for twice the cost you get something just as fast and much more durable. In late game, you may not use him at all due to his bad HP and endurance, only stopping 1 hit from most enemies. [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Dual]] Erasers could be the better option.

==='''True Form'''===
Manic Mohawk Cat gets slightly better health and 8 more speed, making him one of the fastest meatshields by far. He still gets one-shotted by many enemies though. However, this is enough to make him one of the best meatshields, and a staple in mid and late-game, where he can quickly dash to the frontline and stop a hit in time for your other units to live.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield}}

